From 7f29054ff9801714fd1051bd8294c59a2bd12c4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:41:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): a chat's go on a human_request card
 ranks it, sizes the queue, and the chat hears if it stays unclaimed

Defect agent-70dc07d1a5 (2026-11-02): David said "go" in a live chat, which unblocked t_01a19e4974912dcf and
promised "a worker will pick it up". The card kept its p0 rank and sat ready for 113 min behind 47 older p0 cards.
kanban_unblock returned only {"status": "ready"}, and nothing told the chat that the card had no worker.

- kanban_unblock (chat/orchestrator path): when the card carried a human_request, its stored priority rises to
  at least 10 (never lowered) and a priority_raised event is logged with reason human_go. Worker requeue grants
  are unchanged.
- The unblock result carries queue (kanban_queue_position.position), plus queue_hint "bump priority, re-place,
  or do it in this chat; don't promise a pickup" when ahead >= the host's slots, or when the card is unplaceable.
- kanban_chat_wait.sweep (every dispatcher tick): a chat-owned card ready and unclaimed for 30 min to 6 h gets ONE
  chat_wait_unclaimed event per ready episode. The gateway (wakes) and the TUI notifiers deliver it, and it reuses
  kanban_parent_unclaimed.post_notice, which now takes a kind.

Root (happened): live-chat approvals got no rank, and the unblock result hid the queue.
Root (not caught): no notice reached a chat waiting directly on an unclaimed card. e705d05c715 covered only
dependency waits.
